+<para>
+The <literal>bucket</literal> parameter (1.31.12) sets the precision with which
+average times are compared:
+averages are rounded up to a multiple of the specified
+<value>time</value>, and servers with equal rounded averages are
+considered equally fast.
+By default, the precision is 20 milliseconds.
+With servers that respond faster than that,
+a smaller value, for example, <literal>5ms</literal>, allows
+the faster servers to receive proportionally more requests.
+</para>
+
+<para>
+The <literal>smooth</literal> parameter (1.31.12) sets a
+<value>time</value> over which average times are smoothed.
+Each response is given the weight of the fraction of this time elapsed
+since the previous one, but not less than 0.01.
+This keeps averages of busy servers stable, for example,
+when fast and slow requests are mixed,
+while averages of servers with few requests still follow changes
+within about the specified time.
+By default, each response has the weight of 0.05.
+The value of <literal>3s</literal> is a good starting point
+when using a small <literal>bucket</literal>.
+</para>
+
 <para>
